    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1218">

                <pb facs="1159" n="1147" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg1147"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.00N/38½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by President Roosevelt to the Under
                        Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-05-20">May 20, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The enclosed dispatch<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1218-f1"/> worries me. Is there some
                    way in which the Ministry of Uruguay in Washington and Mr. Wilson in Montevideo
                    can get word to the Uruguayan Government that the United States is concerned and
                    that it would be a pity for Pan American solidarity if reports of this kind were
                    to get into the public press, whether they are true or not?</p>
                <closer><signed>F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">rankun</hi>] D. R[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">oosevelt</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
